Most Asked Kubernetes Interview Questions (Based on Recent Experience)

 
🔹 1. How do you handle OOM (Out-Of-Memory) issues or image handling issues in Kubernetes?
Interviewers expect you to talk about memory limits/requests, resource tuning, monitoring using metrics-server/Prometheus, and debugging failed containers.

🔹 2. If Docker images are deleted from the registry but pods are already running from those images — what happens to the cluster?
(They expect an understanding of how nodes cache images and what happens during redeploy or rescheduling.)

🔹 3. What are headless services? What are the use cases?
This checks your understanding of service discovery, stateful workloads, and DNS-based pod access.

🔹 4. In your project:
How many microservices do you have?
How many nodes are used?
How do pods communicate with each other?
 This evaluates real-time system architecture and cluster design.

🔹 5. Write a deployment file that includes:
A deployment
A service
A pod using a Persistent Volume + Persistent Volume Claim
 A hands-on YAML challenge to evaluate your practical Kubernetes skills.
💼 Manager-Level Kubernetes Questions I Encountered
These were asked to evaluate decision-making, architectural thinking, and cost optimization:

🔸 6. How do you design a Kubernetes cluster for high availability and resilience?
(Expectations: multi-master setup, autoscaling, node pools, regional failover.)

🔸 7. How do you plan capacity and optimize cloud costs in a Kubernetes environment?
Topics: right-sizing nodes, spot instances, VPA/HPA usage, cluster autoscaler, monitoring waste.

🔸 8. How do you ensure security and compliance at scale in Kubernetes?
Interviewers look for: RBAC, network policies, secrets management, pod security standards, image scanning, zero-trust networking.

💡 These questions helped me understand which areas to strengthen — especially resource management, HA design, security, and storage.
If you’re preparing for Kubernetes or DevOps interviews, make sure you are confident in:
 ✔️ Pod lifecycle & troubleshooting
 ✔️ Networking & Services
 ✔️ Headless services & StatefulSets
 ✔️ Persistent storage
 ✔️ Cluster architecture & HA
 ✔️ Security & RBAC
 ✔️ Resource planning & cost optimization
 ✔️ Real-time project explanation
